WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.793 --> 00:00:17.897
Perda landed in front of the Wormwood tree, near a rickety hut where a skinny old woman was

2
00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:21.758
stirring an enormous metal pot of foul-smelling stew.

3
00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:24.479
Or was it a potion of some sort?

4
00:00:25.499 --> 00:00:29.040
The people of Wormwood were known to practice some strange magic.

5
00:00:29.716 --> 00:00:35.359
A furry striped creature was stretched out beside the pot, soaking in the warmth of the fire that

6
00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:35.819
heated it.

7
00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:41.881
Perda recognized it as an itchetch, a creature from another world that some people kept as a pet.

8
00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:47.284
But Perda wasn't interested in the woman or her stewpot or even the itchetch.

9
00:00:48.024 --> 00:00:49.305
She stared at the tree.

10
00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:56.388
Its gnarled old branches stretched over the entire area, casting weird-shaped patches of shade.

11
00:00:57.176 --> 00:01:02.380
"It's strange to think that all the magic in Magica came from one tree," Perda thought.

12
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.961
"I can't wait to find out more!"

13
00:01:05.722 --> 00:01:09.765
As she took a step toward the tree, she heard a loud splash right behind her.

14
00:01:09.785 --> 00:01:12.066
"Ouch!" Zann cried.

15
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:17.970
She turned to see that Zann had landed with one foot in the old woman's stewpot.

16
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:22.513
"Drat," Zann muttered, pulling his foot out of the bubbling stew.

17
00:01:23.574 --> 00:01:26.116
Zing was just outside the pot beside Zann.

18
00:01:27.084 --> 00:01:31.027
When the itchetch spotted the dragon, it growled and jumped to its feet.

19
00:01:31.928 --> 00:01:34.570
Zing spit out a burst of fire in return.

20
00:01:35.251 --> 00:01:38.333
Zann grabbed Zing to keep him away from the itchetch.

21
00:01:38.353 --> 00:01:42.797
"Sorry," he added when he noticed the old woman glaring at him.

22
00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:46.360
"That's just like a Red," she spit out.

23
00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.143
"Carelessly ruining a poor old Void's dinner!"

24
00:01:51.104 --> 00:01:52.145
Perda hurried over.

25
00:01:52.165 --> 00:01:55.548
"Please forgive him," she said to the old woman.

26
00:01:56.224 --> 00:01:58.846
"We can fix your, um, soup?"

27
00:01:59.727 --> 00:02:02.729
Just then Gliss and Darb landed, holding hands.

28
00:02:02.749 --> 00:02:04.471
"What's going on?"

29
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:05.472
Gliss asked.

30
00:02:06.152 --> 00:02:07.994
The Void woman rolled her eyes.

31
00:02:08.014 --> 00:02:11.416
"Great, just what I needed," she said.

32
00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:13.098
"Another Red!

33
00:02:13.638 --> 00:02:18.882
Would you like to come into my hut and destroy my few lowly belongings, missy?"

34
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:21.144
Gliss looked confused.

35
00:02:21.164 --> 00:02:23.346
"Um, no?"

36
00:02:23.366 --> 00:02:25.788
"Is that an itchetch?"

37
00:02:26.092 --> 00:02:26.633
Darb said.

38
00:02:26.653 --> 00:02:32.617
"Cool!" "Yes," the old woman said.

39
00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:34.919
"Be careful of your dragon.

40
00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:38.241
My itchetch hates all scaly creatures.

41
00:02:39.062 --> 00:02:43.325
And now that our dinner is ruined, he'll be looking for something else to eat."

42
00:02:44.365 --> 00:02:45.726
She glared at Zing.

43
00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.129
"I'd better do something," Perda thought.

44
00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.172
She rubbed her hands together to make lots of magic friction.

45
00:02:53.988 --> 00:03:00.651
Then she quickly created a whole new pot of delicious-smelling stew, along with a platter of fruit and

46
00:03:00.711 --> 00:03:03.712
cheese. The old woman's eyes lit up.

47
00:03:04.652 --> 00:03:10.595
"Ah, that's more like it," she said, greedily stuffing a piece of fruit into her mouth.

48
00:03:10.615 --> 00:03:12.776
"Apology accepted."

49
00:03:12.796 --> 00:03:14.936
"Good. Let's get out of here."

50
00:03:15.757 --> 00:03:20.259
Zann hurried away, carrying Zing, who was still glaring at the itchetch.

51
00:03:20.839 --> 00:03:23.380
Perda walked closer to the tree's giant trunk.

52
00:03:24.108 --> 00:03:26.669
"Look out for the wormhole," Gliss warned.

53
00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:32.531
Perda nodded, sidestepping the spot so she wouldn't accidentally open the wormhole.

54
00:03:33.392 --> 00:03:39.514
Unlike many of the wormholes in Magica, which appeared and disappeared from time to time, the Wormwood wormhole

55
00:03:39.754 --> 00:03:44.396
had been in the same spot in front of this tree for as long as anyone could remember.

56
00:03:45.397 --> 00:03:47.778
Zann set Zing down and dropped the harness.

57
00:03:48.378 --> 00:03:53.400
Then he snapped his fingers and healed the burns the hot stew had left on his leg.

58
00:03:54.124 --> 00:03:56.225
He also dried his pants and shoe.

59
00:03:59.886 --> 00:04:00.846
out," Darb said.

60
00:04:00.866 --> 00:04:02.546
"Here comes that itchetch."

61
00:04:03.487 --> 00:04:05.107
Zing saw the creature coming too.

62
00:04:05.887 --> 00:04:10.468
He flapped his wings, flying toward the itchetch before Zann could grab his leash.

63
00:04:10.488 --> 00:04:13.949
"Will that thing really try to eat Zing?"

64
00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:15.950
Gliss asked, looking worried.

65
00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.031
"I doubt it," Darb said.

66
00:04:18.051 --> 00:04:20.171
"For one thing, they're about the same size.

67
00:04:20.691 --> 00:04:22.792
See? They're just chasing each other around."

68
00:04:23.616 --> 00:04:25.277
He reached over and took her hand.

69
00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:29.019
"Don't worry, we can keep an eye on them and intervene if we need to."

70
00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.080
Gliss smiled at him.

71
00:04:31.721 --> 00:04:37.183
"Okay." The itchetch tried to tackle Zing.

72
00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.965
But the dragon flew up, shooting flames.

73
00:04:40.825 --> 00:04:45.208
Then he turned and chased the itchetch, causing it to snarl angrily.

74
00:04:45.988 --> 00:04:50.151
Darb knew a lot about animals, so Perda figured Zing would be all right.

75
00:04:50.891 --> 00:04:52.492
She pulled out the blink image again.

76
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.922
"I wonder if this riddle could help to explain how the Source of magic works, like Asta said."

77
00:04:58.942 --> 00:05:03.763
"Maybe," Zann said, leaning in for a look at the words.

78
00:05:04.743 --> 00:05:06.984
He was the only one paying attention to Perda.

79
00:05:07.864 --> 00:05:13.686
Nearby, Darb bent to pick a wildflower, and then he tucked it into Gliss' red hair while she

80
00:05:13.726 --> 00:05:19.127
giggled. Zing and the itchetch stopped running around and started growling at each other.

81
00:05:19.147 --> 00:05:22.068
"'Touch and see,'" Perda said.

82
00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.862
"I wonder what we're supposed to see?"

83
00:05:26.163 --> 00:05:30.006
Zann shrugged, stepping toward the tree and putting a hand on its trunk.

84
00:05:30.026 --> 00:05:32.148
"And what are we supposed to touch?"

85
00:05:32.168 --> 00:05:37.312
"It says 'no need to climb,'" Perda pointed to the words.

86
00:05:37.332 --> 00:05:41.075
"So it's probably something low enough to reach."

87
00:05:41.095 --> 00:05:43.877
"Maybe we should—Zing, look out!"

88
00:05:44.258 --> 00:05:44.918
Zann cried.

89
00:05:45.859 --> 00:05:48.461
The itchetch had just leaped at the dragon again.

90
00:05:49.262 --> 00:05:51.704
Zing was flying backward, shooting flames.

91
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.760
"Huh?" Perda thought.

92
00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:58.002
"The itchetch's claws look sharp, but Zing is pretty tough."

93
00:05:59.162 --> 00:06:02.083
Then she noticed the wormhole swirling open.

94
00:06:02.843 --> 00:06:04.904
For a second she wasn't sure why.

95
00:06:05.744 --> 00:06:08.265
None of them were close enough to open it the regular way.

96
00:06:08.985 --> 00:06:12.846
And none of them were doing magic, which might cause it to open from farther away.

97
00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.747
But that wasn't true, she realized.

98
00:06:16.547 --> 00:06:19.428
It took magic energy for Zing to create fire.

99
00:06:20.156 --> 00:06:25.539
His energy was causing the wormhole to open—and now he was hurtling straight toward it!

100
00:06:25.559 --> 00:06:26.440
"Grab him!"

101
00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.340
Darb shouted.

102
00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:31.863
He started running, but he was too far away to reach Zing in time.

103
00:06:32.663 --> 00:06:34.344
Luckily Zann was closer.

104
00:06:35.204 --> 00:06:39.267
He grabbed Zing's leg just as the wormhole sucked the little dragon in.

105
00:06:39.287 --> 00:06:45.650
"Zann!" Perda cried as she saw him teeter on the edge, trying to pull his pet out of

106
00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:46.951
the swirling wormhole.

107
00:06:47.631 --> 00:06:50.566
She leaped forward, hoping she was fast enough.
